 * `https://bank.example@evil.test` reads as the bank and resolves to the
 * attacker -- and [`parse`](Self::parse) refuses all of those rather than
 * trimming them. So the value on screen is a whole origin or it is nothing,
 * which is the difference between a misleading string and an absent one.
